{%- comment -%}
  The shell (海螺, owner 2026-11-18: "a minimalist conch that connects with our jewellery"). A spiral
  shell in one thin line, with a pearl at its mouth: the sea, then the jewel. On load the spiral draws
  from its centre outwards, the chambers and the lip follow, then the pearl rolls out of the mouth and
  glints; it glints once more a little later. Decorative (aria-hidden). With reduced motion the
  finished drawing shows at once (assets/hikari.css, "The shell").
  Geometry, generated rather than drawn: r = 40·e^(0.26θ) over 2.4 turns, turned 135° so the mouth
  faces down and left; the lip bows out along the spiral's tangent at the mouth, and the pearl sits
  17.6 units along that tangent (--fx/--fy: where it rolls from).
  place: 'above' (under the picture, above the heading) or 'picture' (on the photograph, in white).
{%- endcomment -%}
